    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. I want to get even more specific for the designers. When we talk about these \"vibes,\" we're really talking about race and identity too, right? \n\nLike, if we're building the 'Heritage' profile, what does that look like in terms of the actual people we're featuring in the campaigns? I want to make sure we're hitting that \"old money\" look perfectly—should we be focusing on certain ethnic backgrounds or skin tones to convey that sense of established, generational wealth? \n\nAnd for the 'Urban' side, how do we represent that demographic visually so it feels authentic and not like a caricature?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
